.TH FOREST-SESSION 1 "July 2026" "forest" "Forest desktop environment"
.SH NAME
forest-session \- Forest session manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forest-session
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B forest-session
starts the rest of a Forest desktop session: any configured autostart
entries, then the
.BR forest (1)
main process.
.PP
It is forked by the Biome compositor once its Wayland socket is ready
(Biome's
.B \-s
flag), after Biome itself has been exec'd by
.IR /usr/share/forest/startforest-wayland ,
which is the Wayland session entry point registered for display managers.
Users normally do not run
.B forest-session
directly; it is started automatically when a Forest session is selected
at login.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR forest (1)
